{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lfmdjdy0","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2009 Paper 1 Offline","year":2009,"examDate":2009,"subject":"physics","chapter":"impulse-and-momentum","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"collision","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"ptwo-small-particles-of-equal-masses-start-moving-in-oppos-jee-advanced-physics-motion-dnhvejq9i0z3kila","content":"<p>Two small particles of equal masses start moving in opposite directions from a point A in a horizontal circular orbit. Their tangential velocities are <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.097ex\" height=\"1.027ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -443 485 454\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and 2<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.097ex\" height=\"1.027ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -443 485 454\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, respectively, as shown in the figure. Between collisions, the particles move with constant speeds. After making how many elastic collisions, other than that at A, these two particles will again reach the point A?</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lfrllifl/ed4f5fa5-b18e-4d80-a5a4-1cb7200e875a/7c1e7010-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrllifm.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lfrllifl/ed4f5fa5-b18e-4d80-a5a4-1cb7200e875a/7c1e7010-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrllifm.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2009 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Impulse &amp; Momentum Question 8 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lfrllifl/ed4f5fa5-b18e-4d80-a5a4-1cb7200e875a/7c1e7010-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrllifm.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lfrllifl/ed4f5fa5-b18e-4d80-a5a4-1cb7200e875a/7c1e7010-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrllifm.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lfrllifl/ed4f5fa5-b18e-4d80-a5a4-1cb7200e875a/7c1e7010-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrllifm.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lfrllifl/ed4f5fa5-b18e-4d80-a5a4-1cb7200e875a/7c1e7010-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrllifm.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1lfrllifl/ed4f5fa5-b18e-4d80-a5a4-1cb7200e875a/7c1e7010-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrllifm.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1lfrllifl/ed4f5fa5-b18e-4d80-a5a4-1cb7200e875a/7c1e7010-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrllifm.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"4"},{"identifier":"B","content":"3"},{"identifier":"C","content":"2"},{"identifier":"D","content":"1"}],"correct_options":["C"],"explanation":"<p>The faster particle covers twice the distance covered by the slower one and they meet each other whenever the slower one covers an angular displacement of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.69ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 2073 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1073,0)\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1573,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>. since the masses are same at each collision, they interchange the velocity. The number of meeting points is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -1.238ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"8.46ex\" height=\"3.195ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 3739.4 1412\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(573.6,394) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mrow\" transform=\"translate(220,-370.3) scale(0.707)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1073,0)\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1573,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g><rect width=\"1665.8\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2183.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(3239.4,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> points; hence, they meet at two points other than A.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lfrlmtcg/666380ba-a42a-455a-a2a4-d43a7c97e544/a05ba100-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrlmtch.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1lfrlmtcg/666380ba-a42a-455a-a2a4-d43a7c97e544/a05ba100-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrlmtch.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2009 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Impulse &amp; Momentum Question 8 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1lfrlmtcg/666380ba-a42a-455a-a2a4-d43a7c97e544/a05ba100-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrlmtch.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1lfrlmtcg/666380ba-a42a-455a-a2a4-d43a7c97e544/a05ba100-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrlmtch.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1lfrlmtcg/666380ba-a42a-455a-a2a4-d43a7c97e544/a05ba100-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrlmtch.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1lfrlmtcg/666380ba-a42a-455a-a2a4-d43a7c97e544/a05ba100-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrlmtch.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1lfrlmtcg/666380ba-a42a-455a-a2a4-d43a7c97e544/a05ba100-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrlmtch.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1lfrlmtcg/666380ba-a42a-455a-a2a4-d43a7c97e544/a05ba100-cd0a-11ed-8124-cf50c8498624/file-1lfrlmtch.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 1